* A regression fixture for Refal-5 variable kinds in the driving matchers
* (reference 1.3).
*
* `s.` ranges over symbols, and a macrodigit is a symbol: `Const` holds the
* number 7, and `s.N` must bind it. The driving matchers used to accept only
* characters for `s.`, so this program stalled at the constant and left the
* whole residual call behind. The runtime matcher was always right, which is
* what made the disagreement a bug.
*
* The residue is  'v' 7 e.Input

$ENTRY Go {
  e.In = <Run (Seq (Lit 'v' (Const 7)) (In)) e.In>;
}

Run {
  (In) e.In = e.In;
  (Lit s.C t.P) e.In = s.C <Run t.P e.In>;
  (Const s.N) e.In = s.N;
  (Seq t.P t.Q) e.In = <Run t.P e.In> <Run t.Q e.In>;
}
